# RED runs — two causal controls, gate + probe go red, byte-identical restores — 2026-07-31

Excerpts. Both controls mutate a BUILT artifact on disk; each mutation is proven to have
been fully reversed with `cmp` while both the restored file and its backup exist. No
source file is ever modified.

## RED 1 — deleting one of the four /download version surfaces turns the gate red

With three surfaces left byte-intact on the BUILT `site/dist/download/index.html`, delete
only the AfterInstall output line:

    $ perl -0pi -e 's#<span class="ui-code__line">cswarm 0\.1\.4 \(protocol 0\.1\.0\)</span>#<span class="ui-code__line"></span>#' \
      site/dist/download/index.html

    afterinstall output count -> 0   (removed)
    footer line count         -> 1   (still present)
    visible pin + copy payload      (still present — untouched)

Same gate, standalone, against the mutated artifact:

    $ node --import tsx --test site/scripts/download-version.test.mjs
    exit=1
    ℹ tests 6
    ℹ pass  0
    ℹ fail  6

Restore, proven byte-identical while both files exist:

    $ cp /tmp/ev-dl-backup.html site/dist/download/index.html
    $ cmp site/dist/download/index.html /tmp/ev-dl-backup.html   -> identical (cmp exit 0)
    $ sha256sum site/dist/download/index.html
    17998fb01cd8af66104a47a3527e361b791945a787dca8521e58774a923a5aa7  site/dist/download/index.html

Gate rerun against the restored artifact:

    exit=0; ℹ tests 6; ℹ pass 6; ℹ fail 0

## RED 2 — a forbidden sentinel injected into an emitted bundle turns the rg probe red

The discriminating sentinel probe (green log) must be able to fail. Inject
`build:command-core` into a real emitted browser bundle, probe, restore, re-probe:

    target bundle: site/dist/_astro/LiveDashboard.astro_astro_type_script_index_0_lang.J5bGi8lo.js
    $ cp <bundle> /tmp/ev-bundle-backup.js
    backup sha256: 2ad304bafa7eb2af21c9d0a9ce111e745597f81f28f19fd22039c357f74fb56f
    $ printf '\n/*EV-PROBE*/(0,console.log)("build:command-core");' >> <bundle>

    probe after injection:
    $ rg -l -e 'build:command-core' -e 'test:p1-server' -e 'node:crypto' site/dist/_astro --glob '*.js' | wc -l
    1                <- RED: the probe finds the injected sentinel

Restore, proven byte-identical:

    $ cp /tmp/ev-bundle-backup.js <bundle>
    $ cmp <bundle> /tmp/ev-bundle-backup.js               -> identical (cmp exit 0)
    sha256 restored: 2ad304bafa7eb2af21c9d0a9ce111e745597f81f28f19fd22039c357f74fb56f

    re-probe:
    $ rg -l -e 'build:command-core' -e 'test:p1-server' -e 'node:crypto' site/dist/_astro --glob '*.js' | wc -l
    0                <- GREEN again

The rg probe therefore discriminates: 0 on the clean build, 1 on an injected sentinel,
0 after a byte-identical restore. The superseded `grep -c` form (literal `|`) could not
fail and is not evidence.
